<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.berwilson.backup-verify</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__NODE_BIN__/node</string>
    <string>__APP_DIR__/deploy/drive-backup-verify.mjs</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    Reads the newest Drive backup BACK and compares sha256 against the hash the
    uploader recorded in ~/Backups/berwilson/.drive-status.

    ⚠ THIS EXISTS BECAUSE NOTHING HAD EVER READ A BACKUP BACK. §12 has said from
    the start that a backup is not a backup until it has been read back, and
    measured on 2026-10-21 there was no `pg_restore` anywhere in the repo and
    neither copy had ever been verified — 50GB across two machines assumed good
    because backup.sh exited 0. A push reporting success only proves the API
    accepted the bytes, not that the bytes are right.

    ⚠ IT PROVES INTEGRITY, NOT RECOVERABILITY, and the health card says so in
    those words. A real restore needs the age private key, which lives only on
    Richard's MacBook and in his password manager — so this box CANNOT run a
    restore drill, by design rather than by oversight. A green card must never
    be read as "a restore drill passed".

    Sundays 04:00: the 02:30 backup measured 11m52s end to end on 2026-10-21,
    so 04:00 is well clear of it. Weekly rather than nightly because the check
    DOWNLOADS every artifact (~1.8GB) and the Studio's downstream is ~20Mbps —
    nightly would spend ten minutes a day re-proving an unchanged answer. The
    probe treats a verdict older than 10 days as stale, so a missed run shows.
  -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Weekday</key><integer>0</integer>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>4</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/backup-verify.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/backup-verify.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
